up in Russian cuisine, commonly made with bread kvass or beetroot kvass."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-cold-beet-soup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_beet_soup"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine"],["Latvian cuisine","cuisine/latvian-cuisine"],["Lithuanian cuisine","cuisine/lithuanian-cuisine"],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine"],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Beetroot","ingredient/beetroot"],["Kefir","ingredient/kefir"],["Kvass","ingredient/kvass"],["Sorrel","ingredient/sorrel"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Latvian Eats","ref":"site/latvianeats-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"latvianeats.com","note":"English-language blog of traditional Latvian recipes, including a project cooking through old Latvian cookbooks.","url":"https://latvianeats.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Polonist","ref":"site/polonist-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polonist.com","note":"Polish recipes and food culture from a Polish-born writer living abroad.","url":"https://www.polonist.com/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"Polish Your Kitchen","ref":"site/polishyourkitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polishyourkitchen.com","note":"Long-running blog of traditional Polish home recipes.","url":"https://polishyourkitchen.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Savas Kitchen: Ukrainian recipes","ref":"site/savaskitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"savaskitchen.com","note":"Ukrainian-born home cook Nataliia Savas's section of family Ukrainian recipes.","url":"https://savaskitchen.com/category/ukrainian-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Belarusian cuisine","links":[["Angel wings","dish/angel-wings"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Kal